, 1818, 778], "window": [61549, 99948], "confidence": 0.94, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Node 1385 emits a single event (1385->639) at t in [74000,74500]; node 1186 receives a single event (1818->1186) at t in [66000,66500], roughly 7600 units EARLIER. A cascade requires each hop to follow the previous one in time, so 1186's only reception cannot be downstream of 1385's only emission. Confirmed by the fact that 1186 has zero events anywhere in [74100, 99948], so no delta<=600 chain of any length starting at 1385 can terminate at 1186. The apparent connection is a static-path artifact: 1385->639, 778->639, 778->1818, 1818->1186 exist when time is ignored, and 639 is a high-degree hub (156 events) with 108 events after 74100 - so the negative result is not caused by low activity or lack of topological connectivity, but purely by temporal ordering."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoint activity is minimal and temporally mis-ordered:**\n\n- Node 1385 has exactly **1 event** in the whole window: `1385 \u2192 639`, located in [74000, 74500] (steps 02, 07, 11, 14).\n- Node 1186 has exactly **1 event**: `1818 \u2192 1186`, located in [66000, 66500] (steps 02, 08, 12, 15).\n\n**The target's only reception precedes the source's only emission by ~7,600 time units.** Influence cannot flow backwards in time.\n\n**Decisive check:** after 1385's emission (74100 onward), node 1186 has **zero events at all** (steps 18, 19). There is no interaction that could deliver influence to 1186 after 1385 ever spoke, regardless of path length or the 600-unit gap rule.\n\n**Confounder controls:**\n- *Static connectivity exists*: 1385\u2192639, 639\u2190778\u21921818\u21921186 forms an ignore-time path (steps 09, 13, 16, 17). This is the classic false positive \u2014 the path exists statically but is unusable temporally.\n- *Volume/popularity*: 639 is a major hub (156 events, 135 partners; step 10) and the intermediary set logs 108 events after 74100 (step 20). So the absence is not due to a quiet graph \u2014 the relay nodes stay busy, but 1186 is never contacted again.\n- *No triangle/local clustering* support for either endpoint (step 21).\n- Per-decade scans confirm neither node has hidden additional events (steps 05, 06).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_8980b60f\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1385, 1186, 639, 1818, 778],\n  \"window\": [61549, 99948],\n  \"confidence\": 0.94,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1385 emits a single event (1385->639) at t in [74000,74500]; node 1186 receives a single event (1818->1186) at t in [66000,66500], roughly 7600 units EARLIER. A cascade requires each hop to follow the previous one in time, so 1186's only reception cannot be downstream of 1385's only emission. Confirmed by the fact that 1186 has zero events anywhere in [74100, 99948], so no delta<=600 chain of any length starting at 1385 can terminate at 1186. The apparent connection is a static-path artifact: 1385->639, 778->639, 778->1818, 1818->1186 exist when time is ignored, and 639 is a high-degree hub (156 events) with 108 events after 74100 - so the negative result is not caused by low activity or lack of topological connectivity, but purely by temporal ordering.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 57011, "total_output_tokens": 6144, "total_tokens": 63155, "total_latency_ms": 93645, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}